tsrs patch to the vendored vscode-jsonrpc 9.0.2 (MIT, vendored by microsoft/TypeScript@b85298b6a81f under
packages/typescript/vendor/vscode-jsonrpc; applied by npm/sdk/sync-upstream.mjs, original recorded in
npm/tsrs/UPSTREAM.json "patchedFiles").

sendRequest runs inside `new Promise(async (resolve, reject) => ...)`. When writing the request fails (the API
server died: EPIPE / "write after end"), it rejects the request's promise and then rethrows, and that rethrow
becomes an unhandled rejection of the executor's own promise, which terminates Node (default
--unhandled-rejections=throw). The patch drops only the rethrow; the caller still gets the rejection. Seen with
the pinned upstream client too (tsgo or tsrs server killed with requests queued).

--- a/vendor/vscode-jsonrpc/lib/common/connection.js
+++ b/vendor/vscode-jsonrpc/lib/common/connection.js
@@ -1145,7 +1145,9 @@
                     responsePromises.delete(id);
                     responsePromise.reject(new messages_1.ResponseError(messages_1.ErrorCodes.MessageWriteError, error.message ? error.message : 'Unknown reason'));
                     logger.error(`Sending request failed.`);
-                    throw error;
+                    // tsrs patch (npm/sdk/patches/vscode-jsonrpc-send-request-write-error.patch): the request promise
+                    // is already rejected above; rethrowing from this async executor was an unhandled rejection that
+                    // crashed Node when a request was written to a server that had just died.
                 }
             });
         },
